<!--
    The mark as one filled silhouette: the bar with the crescent already taken
    out of it, rather than a bar plus a crescent painted in the background
    colour.

    ic_duskread_mark_ink builds the shape from two paths and relies on the
    second one matching whatever is behind it. That works on an opaque launcher
    icon and stops working the moment the widget's card goes translucent and
    the wallpaper shows through — the crescent would sit there as a solid dark
    blob. An evenOdd hole is no good either: the crescent is wider than the bar
    and crosses its edge, and evenOdd only subtracts a shape fully inside the
    one below it, so the overhanging part would fill in instead.

    So the outline is traced once, through the two points where the crescent
    actually meets the bar's boundary: (4.613, 3.613) on the top cap, and
    (28, 21.856) on the right edge. Those are computed, not eyeballed. The
    viewport is the silhouette's own bounding box, so the shape fills whatever
    box it is given, and being one path it takes a tint.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="28dp"
    android:height="64dp"
    android:viewportWidth="28"
    android:viewportHeight="64">

    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M0,50 L0,14 A14,14 0 0 1 4.613,3.613 A16,16 0 0 0 28,21.856 L28,50 A14,14 0 0 1 0,50 Z" />
</vector>
